<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<kml xmlns="http://www.opengis.net/kml/2.2"><Document>
<name>Spain 2026 — White &amp; Raymond</name>
<description>Barcelona-based trip, Sep 20 - Oct 3 2026. Built around Jessica &amp; Daniel's wedding, Sep 26 at Mas Rosset. All lodging booked; rental car Sep 24-29 from Barcelona Sants. Updated 23 Aug 2026.</description>
<Folder><name>1 · Barcelona — base &amp; sights</name>
<Placemark><name>National Car Rental — Barcelona Sants</name><description>Conf 2131029323. Citroen e-C4 or similar, compact electric automatic. PICK UP Thu Sep 24, 10:30am - RETURN Tue Sep 29, 5:00pm. EUR 235.85, unlimited mileage, Melissa included as a driver. The counter is in the Saba car park on LEVEL -1, not the station concourse: from inside follow signs to underground parking, or from Placa Joan Peiro take the lift down. Open 7:00am-11:00pm daily. Ask at pickup: Type 2 cable in the car, required return charge level, and the prepaid charging option. International Driving Permit required in Spain - one each.</description><Point><coordinates>2.140000,41.379300,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Barcelona Airport (BCN) — Terminal 1</name><description>Land Mon Sep 21, 12:50pm on DL194. Taxi/Uber ~EUR 35-45, 35 min; Aerobus EUR 7.25.</description><Point><coordinates>2.078500,41.297100,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Grand Hotel Central — your base (Sep 21-24 &amp; Sep 29-Oct 3)</name><description>Via Laietana 30, El Born. BOOKED both stays. Sep 21-24 Superior King, conf 1000596775, EUR 1,336.62. Sep 29-Oct 3 Deluxe King, conf 1000596772, EUR 2,361.88. Both cancellable to 24h before. NO PARKING of any kind - nearest are Saba Francesc Cambo (150 m) and Saba Catedral (350 m).</description><Point><coordinates>2.178000,41.385600,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Sercotel Caspe (Raymonds, Sep 22-24)</name><description>Devon, Natasha &amp; Scott. Conf 9093770930507.</description><Point><coordinates>2.179500,41.396000,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Grand Hotel Central (Raymonds, Sep 28-Oct 2)</name><description>Via Laietana 30. Conf 9093864005462. Same hotel as your second Barcelona stay.</description><Point><coordinates>2.178600,41.385900,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Park Guell (park)</name><description>Tue Sep 22. Meet Mirador de Joan Sales 3:15pm, tour 3:30pm. Ref 1411519457 / 1409828785 - confirm which.</description><Point><coordinates>2.152700,41.414500,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Gallo Santo (restaurant)</name><description>Tue Sep 22, 7:00pm group dinner. Vegan Mexican.</description><Point><coordinates>2.156000,41.403000,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Sagrada Familia (basilica)</name><description>Wed Sep 23, 10:15am. Your own general admission, 2 x EUR 26. No tower access.</description><Point><coordinates>2.174400,41.403600,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Sant Pau Recinte Modernista</name><description>Wed Sep 23, 2:00pm self-guided. 12 min walk from Sagrada. Jessi may hold tickets for 5.</description><Point><coordinates>2.174300,41.411800,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Mar Bella (beach)</name><description>Metro L4, 15 min from centre. Naturist section signposted Espai de Bany Nu.</description><Point><coordinates>2.211500,41.399500,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Mercat de la Boqueria (market)</name><description>Off La Rambla. Free entry, counter bars at the back. Go before 2pm.</description><Point><coordinates>2.171600,41.381700,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Santa Maria del Mar</name><description>El Born. Bare Catalan Gothic, built in 55 years. Free most of the day.</description><Point><coordinates>2.181900,41.383900,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Museu Picasso</name><description>El Born. Early work and the Las Meninas series. Book ahead.</description><Point><coordinates>2.180800,41.385100,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
</Folder>
<Folder><name>2 · Girona &amp; the wedding</name>
<Placemark><name>Castell de Santa Florentina (castle)</name><description>Thu Sep 24, 1:30pm. Canet de Mar - 49 km / 46 min from Sants on the C-32. Game of Thrones - Horn Hill. Tickets still not on sale as of late Aug - monitor. Lunch in Canet de Mar 12:15-13:15 before it.</description><Point><coordinates>2.573500,41.598300,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>DoubleTree by Hilton Girona</name><description>Sep 24-28. BOOKED, conf 3526531356 - King with balcony, EUR 734.16. NON-REFUNDABLE advance purchase: cancelling OR modifying forfeits the payment. Same hotel as the Raymonds and the venue for the Sep 25 meet &amp; greet. Carrer Mossen Joan Pons 1. Covered parking EUR 14/day. No on-site EV charging - nearest ~2 km. Rooftop pool for the Sep 27 brunch.</description><Point><coordinates>2.819400,41.985600,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Girona Old Town (Barri Vell)</name><description>Fri Sep 25 free day. Onyar houses, Jewish quarter, Arab baths, Eiffel footbridge, free city walls.</description><Point><coordinates>2.825000,41.987400,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Girona Cathedral (cathedral)</name><description>Widest Gothic nave in the world. The Great Sept staircase.</description><Point><coordinates>2.826500,41.987300,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Mas Rosset (wedding venue)</name><description>Sat Sep 26 - WEDDING. Ceremony 4:00pm. Cornella del Terri, 19.7 km / 18 min from the DoubleTree via the C-66, ~40 km round trip. Rural with no Uber in Girona - but you have the rental car all weekend.</description><Point><coordinates>2.820000,42.070000,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Clos de Basella (winery)</name><description>Mon Sep 28, 12:00pm-3:00pm. Siurana d&#x27;Emporda, in the Alt Emporda - NORTH of Girona, so this is the long way round to Lloret. Vineyard walk, tour, gourmet picnic. Ref 1411134659 / 1411134619 - confirm which.</description><Point><coordinates>2.995090,42.204977,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Besalu</name><description>Alternate, 20 min from Girona. Medieval town across a fortified bridge.</description><Point><coordinates>2.699000,42.199000,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Banyoles</name><description>Alternate. Largest lake in Catalonia, flat 1-hour walk around it.</description><Point><coordinates>2.766000,42.119000,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
</Folder>
<Folder><name>3 · Lloret — one night, Sep 28</name>
<Placemark><name>Hotel Santa Marta</name><description>Mon Sep 28, one night. BOOKED, conf 26082370424 - Premium with sea-view terrace, EUR 355.43, breakfast included. FREE PARKING WITH EV CHARGING - this is where the car charges for the run back to Barcelona. Free spa hour per stay, 10% off treatments. Smart Flex: date change to 7 days before, penalty if cancelled. Pine woods above Santa Cristina beach, 3 km south of town. JESSI AND DAN&#x27;S GROUP ARE HERE THE SAME NIGHT - the Raymonds are not; they drive back to Barcelona after the picnic.</description><Point><coordinates>2.815800,41.693400,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Platja de Santa Cristina (beach)</name><description>The hotel&#x27;s own beach, ~90 seconds down through the grounds - and the BUSY one. Bar, restaurant, sunloungers, events terrace, and its own paid car park off the hermitage road, so it draws day visitors from Lloret too.</description><Point><coordinates>2.817500,41.692800,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Cala Sa Boadella (beach)</name><description>Tue Sep 29 - the one to aim for. 250 m of sand, pines to the water, no road, no buildings, one small chiringuito. ACCESS: the shore route is closed by a long fence, so go up through the Santa Clotilde gardens, along the hermitage road, then a 200 m dirt path down. 15-20 min at a stroll, shaded. Naturist friendly.</description><Point><coordinates>2.822800,41.694400,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Jardins de Santa Clotilde (gardens)</name><description>Tue Sep 29 morning, 10:00-11:30. Clifftop gardens between Fenals and Boadella. 1919, Rubio i Tuduri. EUR 6.10. Open daily 10:00-20:00 in Sept/Oct - the 10am opening is what sets the shape of the last morning.</description><Point><coordinates>2.826200,41.696000,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Castell de Sant Joan (watchtower)</name><description>11th-century watchtower between Lloret and Fenals. Panoramic views.</description><Point><coordinates>2.836000,41.699000,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Castell d&#x27;en Plaja</name><description>The castle on the rocks at Sa Caleta. Neo-Gothic, actually 20th century.</description><Point><coordinates>2.852000,41.701000,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Tossa de Mar</name><description>25 min north on the cliff road. Walled medieval town on the sea.</description><Point><coordinates>2.931600,41.720200,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Marimurtra Botanical Garden, Blanes (gardens)</name><description>20 min south. Clifftop Mediterranean collection, one of the best in Europe.</description><Point><coordinates>2.801800,41.675700,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
</Folder>
<Folder><name>4 · Day trips from Barcelona</name>
<Placemark><name>Dali Theatre-Museum, Figueres (museum)</name><description>Wed Sep 30. CLOSED MONDAYS in September; Tue-Sun 9:30-18:00. AVE 55-65 min from Sants.</description><Point><coordinates>2.959800,42.268600,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Figueres-Vilafant station</name><description>AVE arrival. 20 min walk or 5 min taxi to the museum.</description><Point><coordinates>2.942000,42.260600,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Montserrat</name><description>Fri Oct 2, after the goodbyes. R5 from Pl. Espanya then rack railway or cable car.</description><Point><coordinates>1.838000,41.593400,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Sitges</name><description>Alternate. R2 from Passeig de Gracia, 35 min.</description><Point><coordinates>1.811700,41.235100,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Balmins beach, Sitges</name><description>10 min walk north from Sitges centre, past the church and cemetery. Clothing optional.</description><Point><coordinates>1.822500,41.240000,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Penedes - Sant Sadurni d&#x27;Anoia</name><description>Alternate. Cava cellars, 45 min by train.</description><Point><coordinates>1.786000,41.427000,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Tarragona</name><description>Alternate. Roman amphitheatre above the beach, 1h by train.</description><Point><coordinates>1.244500,41.118900,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Cadaques</name><description>Alternate. Needs a car - 1h past Figueres. Portlligat is Dali&#x27;s actual house.</description><Point><coordinates>3.277000,42.288700,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Arenys de Mar - La Musclera</name><description>Alternate. R1 train, 50 min. 620m of sand, showers and a beach bar.</description><Point><coordinates>2.545000,41.581000,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
</Folder>
